    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d576">

                <pb facs="0814" n="734" xml:id="pg734"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">648L.113/10a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bingham</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 1460</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1936-10-13">October 13,
                        1936</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: With reference to the Embassy’s despatch
                    No. 2466, dated August 18, 1936, entitled “Proposed Preferential Margin of Duty
                    on Tobacco Imported into Nigeria and the Gold Coast” there is enclosed a copy of
                    a memorandum of a conversation between Mr. Dunn and Mr. H. O. Chalkley, British
                    Commercial Counselor held September 21, 1936,<anchor n="4" xml:id="d576-f1"/> on
                    the same subject.</p>
                <p>There is also enclosed a copy of a memorandum prepared in the Bureau of
                    Agricultural Economics, Department of Agriculture,<anchor n="5" xml:id="d576-f2"
                    /> and dealing with the West African trade in tobacco.</p>
                <p>You are requested, if opportunity presents itself, to supplement by informal
                    reference to the subject the expression of concern which has been conveyed
                    through Mr. Chalkley, and to report to the Department on the results thereof,
                    and to submit any other available information on the whole question.</p>
                <p>Very truly yours,</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>R. <hi rendition="#small-caps">Walton Moore</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
